      "body": "Tested ACK ba7734b\n\nReproduced #36934. On master, `ensure_for` check fails immediately, and on this branch it passes. \n\nAlso checked the new assertion still fails when the backoff is genuinely missing. Set `RECONNECT_TIMEOUT_START` to 0.0 and rebuilding:\n```\ntest_oversized_line: AssertionError: 0.013399518000369426 < 0.5\ntest_overmany_lines: AssertionError: 0.013552839998737909 < 0.5 (run on its own)\n```\nClearly, almost all of the 0.5s threshold has to come from the node's actual wait.\n\nRan `feature_torcontrol.py` 5 times on this branch with backoff restored, all passing.\n\n",
